    "c3"
   ],
   "spoken": "White tries the gambit move order — the pawn to c3, offering the Smith-Morra. There is no need to grab it and play into White's development lead.",
   "kind": "main",
   "teaches": "You don't have to accept a gambit — a sound decline can sidestep the attacker's whole idea.",
   "plans": "Decline by transposing to a structure you know."
  },
  {
   "ply": 6,
   "t": 61,
   "fen": "rnbqkb1r/pp1ppppp/5n2/8/3pP3/2P5/PP3PPP/RNBQKBNR w KQkq - 1 4",
   "line": [
    "Nf6"
   ],
   "spoken": "The knight to f6 is the antidote: it declines the Morra and transposes straight into an Alapin structure, where White has no dangerous gambit — just an ordinary position.",
   "kind": "main",
   "teaches": "Nf6 here converts the Smith-Morra into a harmless Alapin — refute the gambit by transposition.",
   "plans": "Reach the familiar Alapin and equalise comfortably."
  },
  {
   "ply": 7,
   "t": 64,
   "fen": "rnbqkb1r/pp1ppppp/5n2/4P3/3p4/2P5/PP3PPP/RNBQKBNR b KQkq - 0 4",
   "line": [
    "e5"
   ],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
